CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) is a stylesheet language used to describe the presentation and visual formatting of HTML documents. It controls layout, colors, fonts, spacing, and visual effects.

CSS Shadow Effects:
- text-shadow: Adds shadow to text. Syntax: text-shadow: h-offset v-offset blur color;
- box-shadow: Adds shadow to an element (div, container). Syntax: box-shadow: h-offset v-offset blur color;

HTML + CSS Script:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>CSS Shadow Demo</title>
  <style>
    #div1 {
      width: 300px;
      padding: 20px;
      box-shadow: 10px 10px 5px blue;
      font-size: 24px;
      text-shadow: 3px 2px 2px green;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="div1">CSIT Exam</div>
</body>
</html>
```
Explanation:
- text-shadow: 3px (horizontal) 2px (vertical) 2px (blur) green — applies green shadow to the text 'CSIT Exam'.
- box-shadow: 10px (horizontal) 10px (vertical) 5px (blur) blue — applies blue shadow to the div container.

jQuery Selectors are used to select HTML elements to manipulate them. They are based on CSS selectors.
Common selectors:
- $('*') — all elements
- $('#id') — element with specific id
- $('.class') — elements with a class
- $('element') — all elements of a tag type
- $('[attribute]') — elements with an attribute

Callback: A callback is a function executed after the current effect/animation finishes. This prevents running code before an effect completes.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.6.0/jquery.min.js"></script>
  <script>
    $(document).ready(function(){
      $("#btn").click(function(){
        $("#box").hide(1000, function(){
          alert("Box is now hidden!"); // callback runs after hide completes
        });
      });
    });
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="box" style="width:200px;height:100px;background:lightblue;">Hello</div>
  <button id="btn">Hide</button>
</body>
</html>
```

Chaining: Chaining allows multiple jQuery methods to be chained on the same element in a single statement, reducing code and improving performance.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <script src="https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.6.0/jquery.min.js"></script>
  <script>
    $(document).ready(function(){
      $("#btn").click(function(){
        $("#box").css("color","red").slideUp(1000).slideDown(1000);
        // chaining: css -> slideUp -> slideDown on same element
      });
    });
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="box" style="width:200px;height:100px;background:lightyellow;">jQuery Chaining</div>
  <button id="btn">Animate</button>
</body>
</html>
```

