Cookie:
A cookie is a small piece of data stored on the client's (user's) browser by the web server. Cookies are used to:
- Remember user preferences.
- Track user sessions.
- Store login information.
Cookies are sent with every HTTP request to the server automatically.

PHP setcookie() Syntax:
setcookie(name, value, expiry, path, domain, secure, httponly)

```php
<?php
// Create/Set a cookie
setcookie("username", "RamSharma", time() + (86400 * 7), "/");
// name='username', value='RamSharma', expires in 7 days, path='/' (whole site)
setcookie("userlevel", "admin", time() + (86400 * 7), "/");

echo "Cookie has been set!<br>";

// Retrieve a cookie
if (isset($_COOKIE['username'])) {
    echo "Welcome back, " . $_COOKIE['username'] . "!<br>";
    echo "Your level: " . $_COOKIE['userlevel'] . "<br>";
} else {
    echo "No cookie found. Please reload the page to see the cookie.";
}

// Delete a cookie (set expiry in the past)
// setcookie("username", "", time() - 3600, "/");
?>
```
Note: Cookies must be set before any HTML output is sent (before <!DOCTYPE> tag). Cookie values are accessible via the $_COOKIE superglobal array.

text-overflow Property:
The CSS text-overflow property specifies how overflowed text content that is not displayed should be signaled to the user. It only works when:
- overflow is set to hidden (or scroll).
- white-space is set to nowrap (to prevent text wrapping).

Values:
- clip: Clips (hides) the overflowing text abruptly without any indicator.
- ellipsis: Displays '...' (three dots) to indicate that text has been truncated.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>text-overflow Demo</title>
  <style>
    .clip-text {
      width: 200px;
      white-space: nowrap;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: clip;
      border: 1px solid black;
      padding: 5px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    .ellipsis-text {
      width: 200px;
      white-space: nowrap;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      border: 1px solid black;
      padding: 5px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h2>text-overflow Demo</h2>
  <p>Using clip:</p>
  <div class="clip-text">This is a very long text that will be clipped abruptly.</div>
  <p>Using ellipsis:</p>
  <div class="ellipsis-text">This is a very long text that will show ellipsis at the end.</div>
</body>
</html>
```
clip: cuts text off. ellipsis: shows '...' where text is cut off.

