DOM Access Methods:
1. getElementById(id): Returns the single element with the specified id attribute. Returns null if not found.
2. getElementsByTagName(tag): Returns an HTMLCollection (array-like) of all elements with the specified tag name.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>DOM Access Demo</title>
  <script>
    function changeById() {
      // getElementById returns a single element
      var elem = document.getElementById('myPara');
      elem.style.color = 'blue';
      elem.innerHTML = 'Changed via getElementById!';
    }
    function changeByTag() {
      // getElementsByTagName returns collection of all <p> elements
      var paras = document.getElementsByTagName('p');
      for (var i = 0; i < paras.length; i++) {
        paras[i].style.backgroundColor = 'lightyellow';
      }
      document.getElementById('info').innerHTML =
        'Total paragraphs found: ' + paras.length;
    }
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <p id="myPara">This paragraph has id=myPara.</p>
  <p>Second paragraph (no id).</p>
  <p>Third paragraph (no id).</p>
  <p id="info"></p>
  <button onclick="changeById()">Change by ID</button>
  <button onclick="changeByTag()">Change all P tags</button>
</body>
</html>
```

CSS Position Property:
The position property specifies the type of positioning method for an HTML element.

Values:
- static (default): Positioned according to the normal document flow. top/left/right/bottom have no effect.
- relative: Positioned relative to its normal position. Offset with top/left/right/bottom.
- absolute: Positioned relative to the nearest positioned ancestor (not static). Removed from normal flow.
- fixed: Positioned relative to the browser viewport. Stays in place when scrolling.
- sticky: Switches between relative and fixed based on scroll position.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>CSS Position Demo</title>
  <style>
    .static-div {
      position: static;
      background: lightgray;
      padding: 10px;
      margin: 5px;
    }
    .relative-div {
      position: relative;
      top: 20px;
      left: 30px;
      background: lightblue;
      padding: 10px;
      margin: 5px;
    }
    .absolute-div {
      position: absolute;
      top: 100px;
      left: 300px;
      background: lightgreen;
      padding: 10px;
      width: 200px;
    }
    .fixed-div {
      position: fixed;
      bottom: 10px;
      right: 10px;
      background: lightyellow;
      padding: 10px;
      border: 1px solid black;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="static-div">Static Div (default flow)</div>
